bank registers. Exact conditional termination, close pulse balance and hold latching are recorded. Parallel constructor checks and a separate AI scope audit passed; native realization and independent human review remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/source-programme/">Compare the paired programmes →</a></article><article class="claim" id="response-contract-v01"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.4</div><h2>The missing response law is now a typed source contract</h2><p>The finite response fiber has 2^i masks on i intact-null addresses. Count receipts and address receipts have different information requirements. A structural validator and synthetic specimen make the source gate reviewable. The prior presentation review is acknowledged; this new development result awaits independent adversarial review.</p><a class="text-link" href="/source-contract/">Explore the contract →</a></article><article class="claim" id="dependency-update-v03"><div class="eyebrow">14 October 2026 · Reading edition 0.3</div><h2>Polarity and action dependencies</h2><p>Source-bound premises, constitutive choices and evaluation gates now have an explicit scoped graph. Eight change scenarios identify affected uses while retaining conditional mathematics. Absolute clock and native event-source gates remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/dependencies/">Explore the dependencies →</a></article><article class="update-card"><span class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · theorem milestone v0.1</span><h2>A typed gauge-transport construction and its curvature boundary</h2><p>The dedicated theorem manuscript proves local frame covariance, signed tetrahedral relabeling covariance and conserved support for unitary Hasse-link transport. On the filled tetrahedron, a nilpotent transport boundary is pure gauge. Curved transport remains admissible with an explicit correction to the Hodge-square identity.</p><p>A single incidence phase of π/2 gives the exact positive frequency set √2, 2, √6 with multiplicities 1, 5, 1. The result supplies a candidate finite analogue test; it does not derive Standard Model couplings. Independent review and physical correspondence remain pending; physical promotion 0.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#gauge-transport-v01">Read theorem and replay →</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/sources/gauge-transport-v0.1/GAUGE_BRIDGE_CONTRACT_v0.1.json">Bridge contract ↓</a></p></article><article class="update-card"><span class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · source intake v0.1</span><h2>Additional-workstream narrative manuscript captured</h2><p>Review candidate 0.15 is preserved as a separate synthesis with its original PDF hash, complete text extract and page index. Intake preserves source status and leaves scientific replay, independent review and physical correspondence gates unchanged.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#narrative-v015">Read the manuscript →</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/sources/narrative-v0.15/INGEST_RECEIPT_v0.1.json">Intake record ↓</a></p></article><article><time>13 October 2026</time><h3>Receipt gap and common deadline</h3><p>34 write slots; 44 versus 66 total-slot comparisons. Dimensionless probability does not select physical energy or area.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R40">R40 ↗</a></article><article><time>13 October 2026</time><h3>Native signature and refinement</h3><p>Fixed-carrier skew flow does not choose a spatial refinement. Strict unit-readout/intertwining interface fails.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R29">R29 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R30">R30 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R34">R34 ↗</a></article><article><time>13 October 2026</time><h3>POC-1 custody gap</h3><p>Original sidecar bytes and eligible target-hidden native episode remain required before a score.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R35">R35 ↗</a></article><article><time>9–11 October 2026</time><h3>Predictive masks and typed event inputs</h3><p>Structural predicates, current observations and event source laws retain separate roles.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R09">R09 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R28">R28 ↗</a></article></details></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Historical planning snapshot.</h2><details class="atlas-collection"><summary>Inspect the earlier work plan <span>Historical planning, not current status</span></summary></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>The next scientific priority.</h2><p><strong>Source the native event-response law and independently review the corrected conditional domain.</strong> The presentation now exposes every ledger row and its reuse limits. The remaining hinge is scientific: an independently sourced constitutive response, complete proof dependencies and an eligible test. A better reading surface does not supply that law.</p><p>Priority judgment: <strong>96/100</strong>. This score ranks expected progress and information value; it is not a measured closure percentage.</p></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Coverage limitations.</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>One missing image: Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png.</li><li>Nine standalone equation placeholders and 55 placeholder archive entries.</li><li>Raw notebooks include internal/patent material; scientific topics are inventoried.</li><li>Memory crosswalk covers available project context, not all unexported conversations.</li><li>Archived source labels are searchable, but not automatically current.</li></ul><p>Core mathematical checks are exact constructor verification. Human review and physical evaluation remain separate gates. No numerical closure meter is invented.</p></div></section></details></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public 